<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.1.2: Using Product and Quotient Properties for Exponents</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01236</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.1.2: Using Product and Quotient Properties for Exponents</md:title>
    <md:uuid>7b4140db-992b-4af8-aa2b-62f11850c491</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">      <title>Activity</title>
      <note id="note-00001">
        <title>Product Property for Exponents</title>

  <para id="para-00002">If <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>a</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> is a real number and <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>m</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> and <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>n</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> are integers, then</para>
  <para id="para-00003"><m:math>
            <m:mrow>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                <m:mi>m</m:mi>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mi>·</m:mi>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                <m:mi>n</m:mi>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>n</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:msup>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para><para id="para-00004">To multiply with like bases, add the exponents.</para>
      </note>
      <para id="para-00005">Complete problems 1 - 6 using the product property for exponents.</para>
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">

          <para id="para-00006">1. <m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>d</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>d</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00007">Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis>
            button to compare your work.</para>

        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00008">Compare your answer: </para>

          <para id="para-00009"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>d</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>d</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>d</m:mi>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                    <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>d</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00002">

          <para id="para-00010">2. <m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00011">Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis>
            button to compare your work.</para>

        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00012">Compare your answer: </para>

          <para id="para-00013"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                    <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>10</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00003">
        <problem id="prob-00003">

          <para id="para-00014">3. <m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>k</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>k</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00015">Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis>
            button to compare your work.</para>

        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00016">Compare your answer: </para>

          <para id="para-00017"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>k</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>k</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>k</m:mi>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                    <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>k</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>8</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00004">
        <problem id="prob-00004">

          <para id="para-00018">4. <m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mi>v</m:mi>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mi>v</m:mi>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00019">Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis>
            button to compare your work.</para>

        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
          <para id="para-00020">Compare your answer: </para>

          <para id="para-00021"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mi>v</m:mi>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mi>v</m:mi>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mi>v</m:mi>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                    <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mi>v</m:mi>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00005">
        <problem id="prob-00005">

          <para id="para-00022">5. <m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00023">Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis>
            button to compare your work.</para>

        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00005">
          <para id="para-00024">Compare your answer: </para>

          <para id="para-00025"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                    <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>8</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00006">
        <problem id="prob-00006">

          <para id="para-00026">6. <m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mi>p</m:mi>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mi>p</m:mi>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>8</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00027">Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis>
            button to compare your work.</para>

        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00006">
          <para id="para-00028">Compare your answer: </para>

          <para id="para-00029"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mi>p</m:mi>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mi>p</m:mi>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>8</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mi>p</m:mi>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                    <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>8</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mi>p</m:mi>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>14</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <note id="note-00002">
        <title>Product Quotient for Exponents</title>
    
  <para id="para-00031">If <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>a</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> is a real number, <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>a</m:mi>
              <m:mo>≠</m:mo>
              <m:mn>0</m:mn>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>, and <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>m</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> and <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>n</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> are integers, then</para>
  <para id="para-00032"><m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                    <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                  </m:msup>
                </m:mrow>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                    <m:mi>n</m:mi>
                  </m:msup>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>n</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:msup>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>
        , <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>m</m:mi>
              <m:mo>&gt;</m:mo>
              <m:mi>n</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> and <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                    <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                  </m:msup>
                </m:mrow>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                    <m:mi>n</m:mi>
                  </m:msup>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:mi>n</m:mi>
                      <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                      <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                    </m:mrow>
                  </m:msup>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>
        , <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>n</m:mi>
              <m:mo>&gt;</m:mo>
              <m:mi>m</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
  <para id="para-00033">To
        divide with like bases, subtract the exponents.</para>
      </note>


      <para id="para-00034">Complete problems 7 - 12 using the quotient property for exponents.</para>
      <exercise id="exer-00007">
        <problem id="prob-00007">

          <para id="para-00035">7. <m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                      <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                      <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00036">Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis>
            button to compare your work.</para>

        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00007">
          <para id="para-00037">Compare your answer: </para>

          <para id="para-00038"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                      <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                      <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                    <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00008">
        <problem id="prob-00008">

          <para id="para-00039">8. <m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mi>r</m:mi>
                      <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>r</m:mi>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00040">Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis>
            button to compare your work.</para>

        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00008">
          <para id="para-00041">Compare your answer: </para>

          <para id="para-00042"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mi>r</m:mi>
                      <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>r</m:mi>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>r</m:mi>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                    <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>r</m:mi>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00009">
        <problem id="prob-00009">

          <para id="para-00043">9. <m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mi>q</m:mi>
                      <m:mn>9</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mi>q</m:mi>
                      <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00044">Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis>
            button to compare your work.</para>

        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00009">
          <para id="para-00045">Compare your answer: </para>

          <para id="para-00046"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mi>q</m:mi>
                      <m:mn>9</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mi>q</m:mi>
                      <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>q</m:mi>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>9</m:mn>
                    <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>q</m:mi>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00010">
        <problem id="prob-00010">

          <para id="para-00047">10. <m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                    <m:mi>u</m:mi>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                      <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                    <m:mi>u</m:mi>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                      <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00048">Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis>
            button to compare your work.</para>

        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00010">
          <para id="para-00049">Compare your answer: </para>

          <para id="para-00050"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                    <m:mi>u</m:mi>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                      <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                    <m:mi>u</m:mi>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                      <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mi>u</m:mi>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                    <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mi>u</m:mi>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00011">
        <problem id="prob-00011">

          <para id="para-00051">11. <m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mi>j</m:mi>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                      <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mi>j</m:mi>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                      <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00052">Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis>
            button to compare your work.</para>

        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00011">
          <para id="para-00053">Compare your answer: </para>

          <para id="para-00054"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mi>j</m:mi>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                      <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mi>j</m:mi>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                      <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>j</m:mi>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                    <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>j</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00012">
        <problem id="prob-00012">

          <para id="para-00055">12. <m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                    <m:mi>z</m:mi>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                      <m:mn>8</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                    <m:mi>z</m:mi>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                      <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00056">Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis>
            button to compare your work.</para>

        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00012">
          <para id="para-00057">Compare your answer: </para>

          <para id="para-00058"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                    <m:mi>z</m:mi>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                      <m:mn>8</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                    <m:mi>z</m:mi>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                      <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mi>z</m:mi>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>8</m:mn>
                    <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mi>z</m:mi>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
    <note class="self-check" id="note-00003">
      <exercise id="exer-00014">
        <problem id="prob-00014">
          <para id="para-00059"><link class="os-embed" url="#exercise/Alg1_5_1_2_SC"/></para>
        </problem>
      </exercise>
    </note>

    <section id="sect-00002">
      <title>Additional Resources</title>

      <section id="sect-00003">
        <title>Using Product and Quotient Properties for Exponents</title>
        <para id="para-00060">When we combine like terms by adding and subtracting, we need to have
          the same base with the same exponent. But when you multiply and divide, the exponents may
          be different, and sometimes the bases may be different, too.</para>
        <para id="para-00061">First, we will look at an example that leads to the Product Property.</para>
        <para id="para-00062">What does <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mi>·</m:mi>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mn>3</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> mean?</para>
        <para id="para-00063">

          <media alt="An equation shows two x multiplied (2 factors) and three x multiplied (3 factors), separated by a dot, combining to make five x multiplied (5 factors).">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_05_03_05_01.jpg"/>
          </media>

        </para>
        <para id="para-00064">Notice that 5 is the sum of the exponents, 2 and 3. We see <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mi>·</m:mi>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mn>3</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> is <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                  <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:msup>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>
          or <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mn>5</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>.</para>
        <para id="para-00065">The base stayed the same, and we added the exponents. This leads to
          the <term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00001">Product Property for Exponents</term>.</para>
        <note id="note-00004">
          <title>Product Property for Exponents</title>
      
      <para id="para-00067">If <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>a</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math> is a real number and <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>m</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math> and <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>n</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math> are integers, then</para>
      <para id="para-00068"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>n</m:mi>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                    <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                    <m:mi>n</m:mi>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para><para id="para-00069">To multiply with like bases, add the exponents.</para>
        </note>
        <para id="para-00070"><emphasis>Example 1</emphasis></para>
        <para id="para-00071"><m:math>
            <m:mrow>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                <m:mn>3</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mi>·</m:mi>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                <m:mn>4</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                  <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                <m:mn>7</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00072"><emphasis>Example 2</emphasis></para>
        <para id="para-00073"><m:math>
            <m:mrow>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mn>12</m:mn>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mi>·</m:mi>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mn>12</m:mn>
                <m:mn>6</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mn>12</m:mn>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                  <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mn>12</m:mn>
                <m:mn>8</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00074"><emphasis>Example 3</emphasis></para>
        <para id="para-00075"><m:math>
            <m:mrow>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                <m:mn>7</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mi>·</m:mi>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                <m:mn>8</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                  <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>8</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>15</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:msup>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00076"><emphasis>Example 4</emphasis></para>
        <para id="para-00077"><m:math>
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                <m:mi>b</m:mi>
              </m:msup>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>10</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mi>·</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              <m:mi>b</m:mi>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mn>3</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              <m:mi>b</m:mi>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>10</m:mn>
                  <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              <m:mi>b</m:mi>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>13</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:msup>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00078">Now we will look at an exponent property for division. As before,
          we’ll try to discover a property by looking at some examples.</para>
        <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00001">
          <item><para id="para-00107">Consider <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                      <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                      <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>

        <para id="para-00079"><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> - What does it mean?</para>
         <para id="para-00108"><m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00080"><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> - Use the Equivalent Fractions Property.</para>
        <para id="para-00109"><m:math>
            <m:mfrac>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:menclose notation="updiagonalstrike">
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                </m:menclose>
                <m:mo> </m:mo>
                <m:mo>·</m:mo>
                <m:mo> </m:mo>
                <m:menclose notation="updiagonalstrike">
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                </m:menclose>
                <m:mo> </m:mo>
                <m:mo>·</m:mo>
                <m:mo> </m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo> </m:mo>
                <m:mo>·</m:mo>
                <m:mo> </m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo> </m:mo>
                <m:mo>·</m:mo>
                <m:mo> </m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:menclose notation="updiagonalstrike">
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                </m:menclose>
                <m:mo> </m:mo>
                <m:mo>·</m:mo>
                <m:mo> </m:mo>
                <m:menclose notation="updiagonalstrike">
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                </m:menclose>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:mfrac>
          </m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00081"><emphasis>Step 3</emphasis> - Simplify.</para>
        <para id="para-00110"><m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mn>3</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
          </item>
          <item><para id="para-00111">Consider <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                      <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                      <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00082"><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> - What does it mean?</para>
         <para id="para-00112"><m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00083"><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> - Use the Equivalent Fractions Property.</para> 
        <para id="para-00113"><m:math>
            <m:mfrac>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:menclose notation="updiagonalstrike">
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                </m:menclose>
                <m:mo> </m:mo>
                <m:mo>·</m:mo>
                <m:mo> </m:mo>
                <m:menclose notation="updiagonalstrike">
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                </m:menclose>
                <m:mo> </m:mo>
                <m:mo>·</m:mo>
                <m:mo> </m:mo>
                <m:mn>1</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:menclose notation="updiagonalstrike">
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                </m:menclose>
                <m:mo> </m:mo>
                <m:mo>·</m:mo>
                <m:mo> </m:mo>
                <m:menclose notation="updiagonalstrike">
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                </m:menclose>
                <m:mo> </m:mo>
                <m:mo>·</m:mo>
                <m:mo> </m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:mfrac>
          </m:math>
        </para>
        <para id="para-00084"><emphasis>Step 3</emphasis> - Simplify.</para> 
        <para id="para-00114"><m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              </m:mfrac>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
          </item>
          </list>
        <para id="para-00085">Notice that in each case, the bases were the same and we subtracted
          exponents. We see <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                  </m:msup>
                </m:mrow>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                  </m:msup>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>
          is <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                  <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:msup>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>
          or <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mn>3</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>. We
          see <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                  </m:msup>
                </m:mrow>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                  </m:msup>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>
          is <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              </m:mfrac>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>. When
          the larger exponent was in the numerator, we were left with factors in the numerator. When
          the larger exponent was in the denominator, we were left with factors in the
          denominator—notice the numerator of 1. When all the factors in the numerator have been
          removed, remember this is really dividing the factors to one, so we need a 1 in the
          numerator. <m:math>
            <m:mfrac>
              <m:menclose notation="updiagonalstrike">
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              </m:menclose>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:menclose notation="updiagonalstrike">
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                </m:menclose>
                <m:mo> </m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:mfrac>
            <m:mo>=</m:mo>
            <m:mn>1</m:mn>
          </m:math> . This leads to the <term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00002">Quotient Property for Exponents</term>. </para>
        <note id="note-00005">
          <title>Quotient Property for Exponents</title>
      
      <para id="para-00087">If <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>a</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math> is a real number, <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                <m:mo>≠</m:mo>
                <m:mn>0</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>, and <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>m</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math> and <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>n</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math> are integers, then</para>
      <para id="para-00088"><m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                      <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                      <m:mi>n</m:mi>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                    <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                    <m:mi>n</m:mi>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>
          , <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                <m:mo>&gt;</m:mo>
                <m:mi>n</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math> and <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                      <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                      <m:mi>n</m:mi>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mi>n</m:mi>
                        <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                        <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>
          , <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>n</m:mi>
                <m:mo>&gt;</m:mo>
                <m:mi>m</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </note>
        <para id="para-00089"><emphasis>Example 5</emphasis></para>
        <para id="para-00090"><m:math>
            <m:mrow>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                <m:mn>5</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mi>÷</m:mi>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                <m:mn>3</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                  <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00091"><emphasis>Example 6</emphasis></para>
        <para id="para-00092"><m:math>
            <m:mrow>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>k</m:mi>
                <m:mn>9</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mi>÷</m:mi>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>k</m:mi>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>k</m:mi>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>9</m:mn>
                  <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>k</m:mi>
                <m:mn>7</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00093"><emphasis>Example 7</emphasis></para>
        <para id="para-00094"><m:math>
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mi>j</m:mi>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:mn>10</m:mn>
                    </m:mrow>
                  </m:msup>
                </m:mrow>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mi>j</m:mi>
                    <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                  </m:msup>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>j</m:mi>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>10</m:mn>
                  <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>k</m:mi>
                <m:mn>3</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
        <note class="try" id="note-00006">
          <title>Try It: Using Product and Quotient Properties for Exponents</title>
    
      <exercise id="exer-00013">
            <problem id="prob-00013">
              <para id="para-00095">Simplify each expression.</para>
              <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00004">
              <item><m:math>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mn>12</m:mn>
                      <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                    <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mn>12</m:mn>
                      <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math></item>
              <item><m:math>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mn>20</m:mn>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mn>14</m:mn>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:msup>
                    <m:mi>÷</m:mi>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mn>20</m:mn>
                      <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math></item>
                
              <item><m:math>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mi>h</m:mi>
                      <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                    <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mi>h</m:mi>
                      <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math></item>
                
              <item><m:math>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                    <m:mi>s</m:mi>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                      <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                    <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                    <m:mi>s</m:mi>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                      <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math></item>
                
              <item><m:math>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mfrac>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                          <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                        </m:msup>
                      </m:mrow>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                          <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                        </m:msup>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:mfrac>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math></item>
                
              <item><m:math>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                      <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                      <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                        <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                    </m:mrow>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                      <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                      <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                        <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                    </m:mrow>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math></item>
                
              <item><m:math>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mfrac>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                          <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                        </m:msup>
                      </m:mrow>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                          <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                        </m:msup>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:mfrac>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math></item>
                </list>
              <para id="para-00103">Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis>
          button to compare your work.</para>
            </problem>
            <solution id="sol-00013">
              <para id="para-00104">Compare your answers:</para>
              <para id="para-00105">Here is how to simplify the expressions:</para>
              <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00003">
                <item><m:math>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mn>12</m:mn>
                        <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                      <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mn>12</m:mn>
                        <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                      <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mn>12</m:mn>
                        <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                    </m:mrow>
                  </m:math></item>
                <item><m:math>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mn>20</m:mn>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:mn>14</m:mn>
                        </m:mrow>
                      </m:msup>
                      <m:mi>÷</m:mi>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mn>20</m:mn>
                        <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                      <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mn>20</m:mn>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:mn>10</m:mn>
                        </m:mrow>
                      </m:msup>
                    </m:mrow>
                  </m:math></item>
                <item><m:math>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mi>h</m:mi>
                        <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                      <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mi>h</m:mi>
                        <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                      <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mi>h</m:mi>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:mn>11</m:mn>
                        </m:mrow>
                      </m:msup>
                    </m:mrow>
                  </m:math></item>
                <item><m:math>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                      <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                      <m:mi>s</m:mi>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                        <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                      <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                      <m:mi>s</m:mi>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                        <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                      <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                      <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                      <m:mi>s</m:mi>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                        <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                    </m:mrow>
                  </m:math></item>
                <item><m:math>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:mfrac>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:msup>
                            <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                            <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                          </m:msup>
                        </m:mrow>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:msup>
                            <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                            <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                          </m:msup>
                        </m:mrow>
                      </m:mfrac>
                      <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                        <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                    </m:mrow>
                  </m:math></item>
                <item><m:math>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                      <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                      <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                        <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                      <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                      <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                        <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                      <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                      <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                      <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                        <m:mn>9</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                    </m:mrow>
                  </m:math></item>
                <item><m:math>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:mfrac>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:msup>
                            <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                            <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                          </m:msup>
                        </m:mrow>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:msup>
                            <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                            <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                          </m:msup>
                        </m:mrow>
                      </m:mfrac>
                      <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                      <m:mfrac>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                        </m:mrow>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:msup>
                            <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                            <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                          </m:msup>
                        </m:mrow>
                      </m:mfrac>
                    </m:mrow>
                  </m:math></item>
              </list>
            </solution>
          </exercise>
        </note>
      </section>
      <section id="sect-00004">
        <title>Video: Understanding Product and Quotient Properties for Exponents</title>

        <para id="para-00106">Watch the following video to learn more about applying the Product and
          Quotient Properties of Exponents.</para>
